# Security Rules — Non-Negotiable

## Credentials & Secrets
- Zero hardcoded secrets in code — AWS Secrets Manager or env vars only
- .env files never committed — .env.example with placeholders only
- API keys hashed (SHA-256) before storing in DB — never store plain
- JWT private key stored in Secrets Manager — never in code or env file
- Rotate secrets every 30 days via automated Secrets Manager rotation

## PII Protection (TCPA Compliance)
- Caller ANI (phone numbers) encrypted AES-256-GCM before DB storage
- Store ANI as encrypted blob + SHA-256 hash (for dedup only)
- Never log ANI, SSN, DOB, or any caller PII in plaintext
- Call recordings: S3 SSE-KMS, presigned URLs only (15min TTL)
- PII redaction in transcripts before storing (SSN, credit card patterns)

## Input Validation
- Sanitize all inputs before DB operations
- Validate all webhook payloads with Zod before processing
- Verify HMAC signatures on all platform webhooks (Ringba, Retreaver)
- Rate limit all public endpoints via Kong gateway
- Reject oversized payloads (>1MB) at gateway level

## Multi-Tenant
- Never trust tenant_id from request body — JWT header only
- PostgreSQL RLS enforced at DB level — not just application layer
- Redis keys namespaced: {tenant_id}:{key_type}:{id}
- S3 paths include tenant_id: /recordings/{tenant_id}/...

## Network
- All internal service traffic over TLS
- No service directly exposed to internet — Kong gateway only
- Security groups: each service accepts traffic from specific sources only

## Platform Connectors
- Verify X-Ringba-Signature HMAC-SHA256 before processing any Ringba webhook
- Verify signature header for Retreaver webhooks
- Reject unverified webhook immediately with 401
- Log all webhook verification failures with IP and payload hash